    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (78.99) and **Junior Caminero** (76.84) anchoring the lineup, both serving as high-conviction plays. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a favorable matchup against Avila (xERA 4.18) and maintains an elite xwOBA of 0.452, while **Junior Caminero** capitalizes on the softest pitching matchup of the day against Sam Aldegheri (xERA 5.47). Alongside them, **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.58) provide substantial upside in the outfield; both benefit from strong platoon advantages (13-14% boost) and leadoff order spots that maximize their opportunities to secure stolen bases, the scarcity of which remains our primary offensive focal point.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision today involved **Carson Benge** (56.68), who just missed the cut despite a favorable park and wind conditions. While **Carson Benge** provides respectable metrics, the optimization algorithm prioritized the higher floor and consistent platoon matchups offered by **Caleb Durbin** (61.84) and **Luke Raley** (62.51). Meanwhile, **Lars Nootbaar** (50.31) was excluded due to an arduous matchup against Joe Ryan, whose elite SP_xERA of 3.29 significantly dampens the expected offensive output. \n\nRisk management remains a priority given that several hitters, including **Dillon Dingler**, **Gary Sanchez**, and **Trea Turner**, are currently tied to pending lineups. **Trea Turner** is a specific point of concern; despite his high priority, he faces the toughest pitcher of the day in Jacob Misiorowski (xERA 2.79). His base projection took a 19% hit due to this elite SP skill, keeping his score at a modest 49.46. We are cautiously proceeding with our primary starters, but we are prepared to adjust if the confirmed lineups shift our exposure to lower-tier, sub-40 efficiency ratings.",
